{"ocrText": "clari$ the details of the radar obser-\nvations.\nI am grateful to Mr J T Delury of\nthe SRC's Appleton Laboratory for\nsupplying details of the balloon's\nflight.\nReferences:\n1, Bufora Jourrnl Vol 5, No 5, pl (1977).\n2. Flying Saucer Ra;iew Vol 22, No 4, p2\n(re76).\n3. Science Research Council, Annual Re-\nport 1976.\nNew US UFO Probe\nAt the request of President Carter's science adviser Dr Frank Press,\nNASA has agreed to examine UFO records over the last ten years to determine\nwhether the government should launch a full-scale UFO investigation. Dr\nPress, who is director of the Office of Science and Technology Policy has said\nNASA will undertake the study at the request of the Vhite House \" because it\nhas the expertise and facilities.\"\nIn a letter to NASA Administrator Dr Robert Frosch on 2l JuIy 1977,\nDr Press said: \" lVe have discozsered that the White House is becoming the focal\npoint for an inneasing nurnber of enquiries concerning UFOs . . . . . it seerns to me\nthat the focal point of the UFO question ought to be in NASA. Since it has bem\nnearly a decade since the Condon Report, I beline a small panel of enquiry could be\nformed to see if thcre are any significant findings.\"\nMr Herbert Rowe, Associate Administrator for external affairs for NASA,\nsaid a project officer will review cases \" to see if it would be zlorthwhile to conduct\na further inztestigation.\" Walt Andrus, Director of the Mutual UFO Network,\ncalled the NASA involvement \" a oery major step \" in re-opening government\ninvestigation of UFOs.\n******\nOfficial French Government Study\nThe President of the French National Centre for Space Studies-CNES\n-has created an official research group to study the UFO phenomenon. This\nwill include some members of all main Government Research Organisations,\nsuch as the National Centre for Scientific Research, the Astrophysical Institute,\nthe National Meteorology Institute and various universities. The group has\nbeen titled GEPAN-Groupe d'Etude des Phenomenes Aerospatiaux Non-\nidentifies.\nIn efrect since I May, official announcement was withheld to allow time for\nnegotiations with various Research Organisations. Claude Poher, who has been\nhead of the Scientific Systems and Projects Division of the CNES, as well as\ntheir Astronomy Department and their Sounding Rockets Division for a number\nof years is GEPAN's director.", "textLayer": [{"text": "clari$", "x": 6.7, "y": 4.17, "w": 5.95, "h": 2.17, "fontSize": 11.5}, {"text": "the", "x": 12.8, "y": 4.32, "w": 3.4, "h": 1.98, "fontSize": 10.5}, {"text": "details", "x": 16.33, "y": 4.46, "w": 5.84, "h": 1.79, "fontSize": 9.5}, {"text": "of", "x": 22.52, "y": 4.24, "w": 2.37, "h": 2.07, "fontSize": 11.0}, {"text": "the", "x": 25.03, "y": 4.35, "w": 3.4, "h": 1.98, "fontSize": 10.5}, {"text": "radar", "x": 28.62, "y": 4.42, "w": 5.06, "h": 1.89, "fontSize": 10.0}, {"text": "obser-", "x": 33.88, "y": 4.6, "w": 4.95, "h": 1.7, "fontSize": 9.0}, {"text": "vations.", "x": 6.65, "y": 5.89, "w": 6.01, "h": 1.7, "fontSize": 9.0}, {"text": "I", "x": 6.75, "y": 7.21, "w": 1.62, "h": 2.83, "fontSize": 15.0}, {"text": "am", "x": 8.61, "y": 7.87, "w": 3.39, "h": 1.98, "fontSize": 10.5}, {"text": "grateful", "x": 12.19, "y": 7.88, "w": 7.01, "h": 1.89, "fontSize": 10.0}, {"text": "to", "x": 19.54, "y": 7.69, "w": 2.59, "h": 2.26, "fontSize": 12.0}, {"text": "Mr", "x": 22.24, "y": 7.54, "w": 3.64, "h": 2.45, "fontSize": 13.0}, {"text": "J", "x": 25.97, "y": 7.84, "w": 1.89, "h": 2.36, "fontSize": 12.5}, {"text": "T", "x": 27.97, "y": 7.32, "w": 2.5, "h": 2.74, "fontSize": 14.5}, {"text": "Delury of", "x": 30.53, "y": 7.87, "w": 8.62, "h": 2.07, "fontSize": 11.0}, {"text": "the", "x": 6.65, "y": 9.04, "w": 3.88, "h": 2.26, "fontSize": 12.0}, {"text": "SRC's Appleton Laboratory for", "x": 10.66, "y": 9.26, "w": 28.34, "h": 2.01, "fontSize": 10.5}, {"text": "supplying", "x": 6.7, "y": 10.57, "w": 9.6, "h": 2.07, "fontSize": 11.0}, {"text": "details"